// @trap memory access out of bounds
// The offset form does not wrap. `p + 8` is an i32 add, so from p = -4 (0xFFFFFFFC) it wraps
// to address 4 and reads it. `__load_i32__(p, 8)` puts 8 in the memarg instead, and wasm adds
// a memarg offset without wrapping: the effective address is 2^32 + 4, and the load traps.
const p = 0 - 4
__store_i32__(4, 11)
print(__load_i32__(p + 8))
print(__load_i32__(p, 8))
